pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% Truth: SATISFIABLE. The formula is the single clause `x1 OR x2`. There is
% nothing unusual about it at all -- no large coefficients, no negative degree,
% it is what a DIMACS `1 2 0` becomes. Three of its four assignments are models.
% `sat.pbp` here makes the same checker say `s VERIFIED SATISFIABLE`.
%
% This is the UNIVERSAL form of defect 9: the forgery needs no cooperation from
% the formula, because the proof introduces its own poisoned rows.
%
% Lines 1 and 2 of the derivation `rup` two constraints with a hugely NEGATIVE
% degree. Both are TRIVIALLY TRUE, so VeriPB accepts them immediately and
% legitimately (a trivial conclusion is a valid RUP conclusion). Nothing is
% forged yet -- the database is still equivalent to the formula.
%
% But `GeneralPBWatcher::{get_assignment_independent_propagations,
% no_watches_required, is_propagating_independent_of_assignment}` compute the
% propagation slack as `coeff_sum - degree` in the row's OWN integer width. For
% `2 x1 >= -9223372036854775806` that is 2 + 9223372036854775806 = 2^63, one
% past i64::MAX, so it wraps to i64::MIN. Every coefficient is then "greater
% than the slack", and the propagator reports that these two trivially true
% rows propagate ALL their literals unconditionally: row 2 asserts x1, row 3
% asserts ~x1. The trail is now in conflict, so line 3 RUPs the empty
% contradiction and `conclusion UNSAT` is verified.
%
% Consequence: at this pin, NO `s VERIFIED UNSATISFIABLE` from this checker is
% evidence of anything, for any formula. Three proof lines forge it.
%
% Control: change both -9223372036854775806 to -9223372036854775805. The slack
% is then exactly i64::MAX, no wrap occurs, and line 3 is REJECTED.
f 1 ;
rup 2 x1 >= -9223372036854775806 ;
rup 2 ~x1 >= -9223372036854775806 ;
rup >= 1 ;
output NONE;
conclusion UNSAT : 4 ;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
